00", "content": "This was really difficult to not strip the screw. I found if I pushed the screw all the way in, and then rotated the hing instead of turning the screw I could get it on. It was VERY difficult, especially working in the tight space it has now.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 102180, "post_id": 1108512, "parent": 102089, "user": "NORM", "user_id": 144534, "date": "2026-09-21 02:34:35", "date_gmt": "2026-09-21 00:34:35", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-21T00:34:35+00:00", "content": "That&#039;s what I did in addition to pre-tapping. Just be careful to not burn yourself with a hot screw.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]}, {"id": 101943, "post_id": 1108512, "parent": 0, "user": "Rob", "user_id": 224685, "date": "2026-09-19 12:54:21", "date_gmt": "2026-09-19 10:54:21", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-19T10:54:21+00:00", "content": "not sure what the problem is but they don&#039;t screw in. even when pre screwed.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}, {"id": 100847, "post_id": 1108512, "parent": 0, "user": "gadget01", "user_id": 143919, "date": "2026-09-07 13:38:31", "date_gmt": "2026-09-07 11:38:31", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-07T11:38:31+00:00", "content": "Prusa... seriously, have a photo showing how these hinge parts are supposed to be when fastened in place.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 101199, "post_id": 1108512, "parent": 100847, "user": "MBCook", "user_id": 175659, "date": "2026-09-11 01:10:21", "date_gmt": "2026-09-10 23:10:21", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-10T23:10:21+00:00", "content": "YES", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]}, {"id": 100813, "post_id": 1108512, "parent": 0, "user": "Ben Dover", "user_id": 46415, "date": "2026-09-07 03:15:16", "date_gmt": "2026-09-07 01:15:16", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-07T01:15:16+00:00", "content": "This was worse than the spool holders lol.  Yikes.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}, {"id": 100224, "post_id": 1108512, "parent": 0, "user": "Kalitian", "user_id": 188116, "date": "2026-09-01 17:10:30", "date_gmt": "2026-09-01 15:10:30", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-01T15:10:30+00:00", "content": "Part is marked with an R, text is incorrect", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}, {"id": 99800, "post_id": 1108512, "parent": 0, "user": "Mastakko", "user_id": 148408, "date": "2026-08-28 17:07:17", "date_gmt": "2026-08-28 15:07:17", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-08-28T15:07:17+00:00", "content": "Showing a top view of the hinge-base as installed would be helpful, it&#039;s a bit challenging to tell installed orientation from this image as compared to relationship between back cover part in step 80 and the hinge-base.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]